1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:02,169
<i>Previously on Gotham...</i>

2
00:00:02,169 --> 00:00:03,670
You're the brother I never had.

3
00:00:03,670 --> 00:00:06,006
We will create a legacy in this city.

4
00:00:06,006 --> 00:00:09,142
<i>Gotham falls, we rise.</i>

5
00:00:09,142 --> 00:00:10,344
Together.

6
00:00:10,344 --> 00:00:11,511
<i>Poor Jim.</i>

7
00:00:11,511 --> 00:00:12,546
All alone again.

8
00:00:12,546 --> 00:00:13,847
I told you to leave.

9
00:00:13,847 --> 00:00:14,715
I heard you.

10
00:00:15,549 --> 00:00:17,150
<i>So many things I wish I could change.</i>

11
00:00:17,150 --> 00:00:18,352
Things I have done.

12
00:00:18,352 --> 00:00:19,620
We're here now.

13
00:00:19,620 --> 00:00:22,022
We'll try to put the pieces
back together again.

14
00:00:22,022 --> 00:00:23,690
Jim, I'm pregnant.

15
00:00:24,825 --> 00:00:25,859
This isn't you.

16
00:00:25,859 --> 00:00:27,628
We're not the same.

17
00:00:27,628 --> 00:00:29,663
<i>That night that your parents
were murdered,</i>

18
00:00:29,663 --> 00:00:32,966
<i>I didn't do anything
because I didn't care.</i>

19
00:00:32,966 --> 00:00:35,569
Everyone, let's dig a little deeper.

20
00:00:35,569 --> 00:00:39,039
Because that's the only way
you're all making it out of this hole.

21
00:00:39,706 --> 00:00:41,174
Deep enough?

22
00:00:42,242 --> 00:00:43,744
<i>You're leaving Gotham.</i>

23
00:00:43,744 --> 00:00:45,412
<i>There's nothing left for me here anymore.</i>

24
00:00:45,412 --> 00:00:46,713
<i>I've done all I can.</i>

25
00:00:46,713 --> 00:00:47,915
I want in.

26
00:00:49,683 --> 00:00:53,387
I love family reunions.

27
00:00:53,387 --> 00:00:54,221
Don't you?

28
00:01:02,195 --> 00:01:04,197
Go. Go, go.

29
00:01:17,678 --> 00:01:19,012
- Which way?
- Wait.

30
00:01:50,744 --> 00:01:55,816
General, you were the ones who let Walker
operate right under your noses.

31
00:01:55,816 --> 00:01:57,818
Now you're telling me she evaded capture?

32
00:01:57,818 --> 00:01:59,920
<i>I understand your frustration.</i>

33
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:02,789
Have you at least determined
why she did what she did?

34
00:02:02,789 --> 00:02:04,157
<i>Not yet.</i>

35
00:02:04,157 --> 00:02:08,362
Look, bottom line, Walker and Dorrance
are out of the picture.

36
00:02:08,362 --> 00:02:10,664
What else is standing in the way
of reunification?

37
00:02:10,664 --> 00:02:11,631
<i>Nothing.</i>

38
00:02:11,631 --> 00:02:14,935
<i>I'm recommending we begin the process
immediately.</i>

39
00:02:14,935 --> 00:02:17,938
There have been a lot of promises
from across the river.

40
00:02:17,938 --> 00:02:21,808
<i>But unlike Walker or whoever she is,
I have the authority to take action.</i>

41
00:02:21,808 --> 00:02:24,778
<i>Unless something happens
to destabilise Gotham again,</i>

42
00:02:24,778 --> 00:02:27,447
<i>this nightmare is about to end.</i>

43
00:02:27,447 --> 00:02:28,782
<i>Think he's for real?</i>

44
00:02:28,782 --> 00:02:30,283
I'll believe it when it happens.

45
00:02:30,283 --> 00:02:32,486
I take it your search party
didn't find Alfred.

46
00:02:32,486 --> 00:02:34,621
Neither hide nor hair.

47
00:02:34,621 --> 00:02:37,357
Pennyworth vanished five days ago.
It ain't looking good.

48
00:02:37,357 --> 00:02:39,326
How's Bruce?

49
00:02:39,326 --> 00:02:42,195
He's been pulling double shifts
on the search parties.

50
00:02:42,195 --> 00:02:43,663
Kid's dead on his feet.

51
00:02:49,302 --> 00:02:50,637
I wanna search this area next.

52
00:02:50,637 --> 00:02:52,105
There are whole blocks
of abandoned buildings.

53
00:02:52,105 --> 00:02:53,140
I'll get a squad right on it.

54
00:02:53,140 --> 00:02:54,875
Just give me five minutes. I'll be ready.

55
00:02:55,175 --> 00:02:56,476
You're not going out.

56
00:02:56,476 --> 00:02:58,412
- No, Jim--
- You need your rest.

57
00:02:58,412 --> 00:03:01,415
I'm not cutting you out,
but I need you sharp, not a liability.

58
00:03:06,053 --> 00:03:08,422
I just don't understand
what could have happened.

59
00:03:08,422 --> 00:03:10,123
Neither do I.

60
00:03:10,123 --> 00:03:12,959
But I know that Alfred Pennyworth
can take care of himself.

61
00:03:14,694 --> 00:03:16,396
I'll send for you if I hear anything.

62
00:03:24,204 --> 00:03:26,339
- Kid's tough.
- Yeah.

63
00:03:26,339 --> 00:03:29,743
In other good-ish news, Harper radioed.
Her squad found something.

64
00:03:29,743 --> 00:03:30,577
What?

65
00:03:32,379 --> 00:03:33,513
It's weird.

66
00:03:36,083 --> 00:03:37,017
Four men.

67
00:03:38,018 --> 00:03:40,020
Looks like they breathed in some
sort of chemical agent.

68
00:03:40,020 --> 00:03:41,321
I'm thinking airborne.

69
00:03:41,321 --> 00:03:43,523
And the Z's on their bodies?

70
00:03:43,523 --> 00:03:45,358
Carved into them before time of death.

71
00:03:45,358 --> 00:03:46,726
Check out the moustache.

72
00:03:50,597 --> 00:03:51,765
Fake.

73
00:03:51,765 --> 00:03:53,533
Seems like they escaped from here.

74
00:03:56,837 --> 00:03:58,038
A film set?

75
00:03:58,038 --> 00:03:59,206
I said it was weird.

76
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:02,175
Z's on their chests.

77
00:04:02,175 --> 00:04:04,344
Think it could be Zsasz?

78
00:04:05,412 --> 00:04:07,214
Chemicals aren't really his MO.

79
00:04:07,214 --> 00:04:10,250
Plus, I never figured Zsasz
for much of a cinephile.

80
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:11,184
But whoever it is,

81
00:04:11,184 --> 00:04:13,620
if they have more of these chemicals
and the will to use them--

82
00:04:13,620 --> 00:04:15,555
It's bye-bye, reunification.

83
00:04:15,555 --> 00:04:18,859
Gotta stop him before news
reaches the mainland.

84
00:04:21,061 --> 00:04:23,130
The Chessmen.

85
00:04:23,130 --> 00:04:24,931
That's a gang that operates
out of the Narrows.

86
00:04:24,931 --> 00:04:27,067
What the hell is a Narrows gang
doing way up here?

87
00:04:27,067 --> 00:04:29,436
I think we both know someone we can ask.

88
00:06:24,417 --> 00:06:25,885
Can you check on the fever in Bed 12?

89
00:06:25,885 --> 00:06:27,520
What's up, Doc?

90
00:06:27,520 --> 00:06:28,688
Heard you were working here.

91
00:06:28,688 --> 00:06:29,656
Interesting.

92
00:06:29,656 --> 00:06:31,224
It's what I do, help people.

93
00:06:31,224 --> 00:06:33,660
Speaking of which, I've got patients.

94
00:06:33,660 --> 00:06:37,163
Oh, you wouldn't kick Jim's baby mama
to the kerb now, would you?

95
00:06:37,163 --> 00:06:40,200
Whatever happened between you and Jim,
it's none of my concern.

96
00:06:40,200 --> 00:06:42,402
- So if you're here to gloat--
- I'm here for medical assistance.

97
00:06:43,570 --> 00:06:45,572
For my little nugget.

98
00:06:45,572 --> 00:06:47,707
What do you say? Be my OB?

99
00:06:47,707 --> 00:06:50,677
- You can't be serious.
- I know we've had our differences.

100
00:06:50,677 --> 00:06:52,579
You tried to kill me, Barbara.

101
00:06:52,579 --> 00:06:53,780
Twice.

102
00:06:53,780 --> 00:06:55,749
That was years ago.

103
00:06:55,749 --> 00:06:57,450
There are other doctors here.

104
00:06:57,450 --> 00:06:59,252
Not as good as you.

105
00:06:59,252 --> 00:07:01,421
Look, whatever you think of me,

106
00:07:01,421 --> 00:07:03,923
my child is innocent
and I want the best for it.

107
00:07:03,923 --> 00:07:05,859
And in this place, that means you.

108
00:07:09,529 --> 00:07:12,599
- Does Jim know you're here?
- This is none of his business.

109
00:07:12,599 --> 00:07:13,466
Lee?

110
00:07:17,037 --> 00:07:17,971
Jim.

111
00:07:20,240 --> 00:07:22,108
- Barbara.
- You're interrupting.

112
00:07:22,108 --> 00:07:24,110
Doctor-patient. Blow.

113
00:07:24,110 --> 00:07:26,613
- I'm sorry, you're her doctor?
- No.

114
00:07:26,613 --> 00:07:28,315
I don't know. Maybe.

115
00:07:28,315 --> 00:07:29,582
What are you doing here?

116
00:07:30,583 --> 00:07:33,386
Some bodies turned up.
They might have a Narrows connection.

117
00:07:33,386 --> 00:07:34,621
I wouldn't have come but--

118
00:07:34,621 --> 00:07:36,256
It's important. Right.

119
00:07:37,390 --> 00:07:38,758
You two need to talk.

120
00:07:39,759 --> 00:07:41,594
- I'll be outside.
- I'd rather not.

121
00:07:41,594 --> 00:07:44,397
If you want me to be your doctor,
you will talk to the baby's...

122
00:07:44,831 --> 00:07:46,433
father.

123
00:07:46,433 --> 00:07:47,901
Your first appointment is next week.

124
00:07:47,901 --> 00:07:49,903
The nurse will give you all your vitamins
when you leave.

125
00:07:49,903 --> 00:07:50,737
Deal?

126
00:07:59,746 --> 00:08:01,281
Is she really the only one you could find?

127
00:08:01,281 --> 00:08:03,516
She's the best doctor
in this hellhole of a city.

128
00:08:03,516 --> 00:08:04,951
Not everything is about Jim Gordon.

129
00:08:04,951 --> 00:08:06,019
Pretty sure this one is.

130
00:08:06,019 --> 00:08:08,421
Because we slept together. Yeah.

131
00:08:08,421 --> 00:08:10,523
I only told you because I felt
you had a right to know,

132
00:08:10,523 --> 00:08:14,194
but your involvement in this ended
the moment you put your pants back on.

133
00:08:17,964 --> 00:08:18,865
What?

134
00:08:20,333 --> 00:08:22,769
- You don't think I'm fit to be a mother?
- What do you think?

135
00:08:25,472 --> 00:08:26,439
Barbara.

136
00:09:23,930 --> 00:09:25,432
Who are you?

137
00:09:26,599 --> 00:09:28,601
Well, look who decided to join us.

138
00:09:28,601 --> 00:09:29,669
Hello, champ.

139
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:35,442
Master Bruce!

140
00:09:35,442 --> 00:09:37,076
Alfred, how did you...

141
00:09:37,076 --> 00:09:38,545
Look at the state of you.

142
00:09:38,545 --> 00:09:40,613
What have I told you
about rolling around in the muck?

143
00:09:42,048 --> 00:09:43,683
Alfred.

144
00:09:43,683 --> 00:09:45,385
What's going on?
Who are these people?

145
00:09:45,385 --> 00:09:46,786
Whatever do you mean, Bruce?

146
00:09:47,887 --> 00:09:49,522
We're your parents.

147
00:09:51,257 --> 00:09:53,059
Right. Well, let's get you spruced up.

148
00:09:53,059 --> 00:09:56,262
After all, we have a guest.

149
00:10:00,033 --> 00:10:02,368
Welcome home, Bruce.

150
00:10:06,372 --> 00:10:07,407
Jeremiah.

151
00:10:08,575 --> 00:10:09,609
You're alive.

152
00:10:11,711 --> 00:10:15,915
Well, you didn't think Selina
could kill me so easily, did you?

153
00:10:17,650 --> 00:10:22,055
I just had to put you off my scent
until I could finalise my project.

154
00:10:22,889 --> 00:10:24,791
Manners, Master Bruce.

155
00:10:24,791 --> 00:10:26,392
Let's not be rude to our guest.

156
00:10:26,392 --> 00:10:28,728
Especially when I come bearing gifts.

157
00:10:29,796 --> 00:10:32,565
Oh, Mr. Jeremiah. A cake.

158
00:10:32,565 --> 00:10:34,667
How exceedingly kind of you.

159
00:10:34,667 --> 00:10:37,170
Is it Italian meringue?

160
00:10:37,170 --> 00:10:38,471
- Sure.
- Oh.

161
00:10:39,606 --> 00:10:40,840
Now, now, Bruce.

162
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:44,911
You come any closer and I blow up
Wayne Manor with all of us inside of it.

163
00:10:44,911 --> 00:10:48,615
I have a dozen more of these
Italian meringues

164
00:10:48,615 --> 00:10:51,985
sprinkled all throughout the house.

165
00:10:51,985 --> 00:10:54,454
What did you do to Alfred?

166
00:10:54,454 --> 00:10:56,322
And who are these people?

167
00:10:56,322 --> 00:10:58,258
Glad you asked. Come.

168
00:10:58,258 --> 00:10:59,659
Come, come.

169
00:11:01,528 --> 00:11:04,330
Mummy and Daddy dearest

170
00:11:04,330 --> 00:11:10,603
were just an innocent couple I kidnapped
based on bone structure and...

171
00:11:12,472 --> 00:11:14,173
build.

172
00:11:14,173 --> 00:11:18,311
Just a touch of plastic surgery
and voila...

173
00:11:19,612 --> 00:11:20,547
Waynes.

174
00:11:22,181 --> 00:11:24,784
Alfred, I nabbed in the Green Zone.

175
00:11:24,784 --> 00:11:26,519
They're hypnotised.

176
00:11:26,519 --> 00:11:29,989
Well, I'm afraid there was no room
for improv in our script.

177
00:11:29,989 --> 00:11:34,027
Today is a very important day, Bruce.

178
00:11:35,862 --> 00:11:37,897
Just look at the way they're dressed.

179
00:11:41,067 --> 00:11:43,870
It's the night my parents were killed.

180
00:11:43,870 --> 00:11:48,241
And I'm giving you the chance
to experience it all over again.

181
00:11:50,343 --> 00:11:52,979
- Why?
- Isn't it obvious?

182
00:11:56,883 --> 00:11:57,717
Bruce...

183
00:11:59,419 --> 00:12:03,923
this, this was the most important day
of your life.

184
00:12:06,492 --> 00:12:08,428
And I didn't get to be a part of it.

185
00:12:10,763 --> 00:12:12,899
We need to rectify that.

186
00:12:12,899 --> 00:12:14,033
Alfred.

187
00:12:14,033 --> 00:12:15,435
It's time for dinner.

188
00:12:15,435 --> 00:12:18,905
Chop-chop. We're on a very tight schedule.

189
00:12:18,905 --> 00:12:20,540
Of course, Mr. Jeremiah.

190
00:12:39,926 --> 00:12:41,394
That's zero for three.

191
00:12:42,862 --> 00:12:43,963
Yes.

192
00:12:43,963 --> 00:12:47,066
It seems the government was quite thorough
when they mined the river.

193
00:12:47,066 --> 00:12:49,268
You didn't have a plan
to get off this rock

194
00:12:49,268 --> 00:12:51,037
before you stole everyone's crap?

195
00:12:51,037 --> 00:12:54,107
I was working on a plan.

196
00:12:54,107 --> 00:12:55,608
The river is mined.

197
00:12:55,608 --> 00:12:59,812
Everything that flies out
gets blown from the sky.

198
00:12:59,812 --> 00:13:00,647
What?

199
00:13:02,448 --> 00:13:05,118
Jeremiah was digging a tunnel
under the river.

200
00:13:06,719 --> 00:13:07,787
A tunnel?

201
00:13:08,988 --> 00:13:09,989
Really?

202
00:13:09,989 --> 00:13:11,724
Do you have any better ideas?

203
00:13:16,095 --> 00:13:18,498
Didn't think so.

204
00:13:18,498 --> 00:13:20,266
It's in the Dark Zone.

205
00:13:20,266 --> 00:13:22,402
We should wait until night
to check it out.

206
00:13:22,402 --> 00:13:25,238
Well, I was running out
of guinea pigs anyway.

207
00:13:28,074 --> 00:13:30,643
Oh, look.
He's swimming to shore.

208
00:13:38,484 --> 00:13:40,787
Are you sure you should be out
in the Narrows alone?

209
00:13:40,787 --> 00:13:43,456
When the bridges fell,
this place descended into chaos.

210
00:13:43,456 --> 00:13:44,957
Figure our best bet of getting out
in one piece

211
00:13:44,957 --> 00:13:46,426
is to keep a low profile.

212
00:13:46,426 --> 00:13:47,326
So all the work I did

213
00:13:47,326 --> 00:13:49,295
to make the Narrows better
was for nothing.

214
00:13:51,364 --> 00:13:53,700
It's the Leopards,
Rivals of the Chessmen.

215
00:13:55,868 --> 00:13:57,603
It's pretty bad.

216
00:13:59,138 --> 00:14:01,474
- About this Barbara thing...
- Jim, just don't.

217
00:14:01,474 --> 00:14:03,443
No, it's important to me
that you understand.

218
00:14:06,345 --> 00:14:08,648
Okay. So, what are you gonna do?

219
00:14:11,551 --> 00:14:13,453
I don't know but it's my child too.

220
00:14:16,155 --> 00:14:18,624
Barbara seems
to have a difference of opinion.

221
00:14:19,158 --> 00:14:21,027
But, hey, people change.

222
00:14:21,027 --> 00:14:22,328
You don't know her like I do.

223
00:14:22,328 --> 00:14:23,563
You can say that again.

224
00:14:26,232 --> 00:14:27,066
Look.

225
00:14:29,469 --> 00:14:30,369
We're clear.

226
00:14:31,571 --> 00:14:33,306
The Chessmen moved around.

227
00:14:33,306 --> 00:14:35,475
They used these
as signals for their members.

228
00:14:35,475 --> 00:14:36,976
The rook's a compass needle.

229
00:14:36,976 --> 00:14:38,845
North-northeast. Let's go.

230
00:14:55,328 --> 00:14:59,699
Alfred told me such great tidbits
about your childhood.

231
00:14:59,699 --> 00:15:02,568
How you used to eat here in the kitchen

232
00:15:02,568 --> 00:15:04,904
when it was just you and the family.

233
00:15:04,904 --> 00:15:08,875
My, how homey and intimate.

234
00:15:11,110 --> 00:15:12,545
Grilled cheese

235
00:15:12,545 --> 00:15:15,248
and Branston pickle sandwich,
Mr. Jeremiah.

236
00:15:15,248 --> 00:15:16,682
Master Bruce's favourite.

237
00:15:16,682 --> 00:15:22,421
My influence, though, Thomas did add
a dash of aioli for extra flair.

238
00:15:28,928 --> 00:15:30,797
Oh, Come on, Bruce.

239
00:15:30,797 --> 00:15:33,766
That's a weird favourite food
for a 12-year-old.

240
00:15:33,766 --> 00:15:35,201
I'm playing your game.

241
00:15:37,203 --> 00:15:39,205
Now let Alfred and these people go.

242
00:15:39,205 --> 00:15:40,540
They're innocent.

243
00:15:40,540 --> 00:15:43,309
I'm sorry, Bruce, it's just.

244
00:15:43,309 --> 00:15:49,048
It's very important to me
that I get every detail exactly right.

245
00:15:49,048 --> 00:15:52,552
Speaking of which, the final touch.

246
00:16:04,297 --> 00:16:05,598
What was it like...

247
00:16:06,899 --> 00:16:09,068
losing your parents that night?

248
00:16:12,405 --> 00:16:15,007
I lost my family too, Bruce.

249
00:16:16,676 --> 00:16:18,744
The wound still hasn't healed.

250
00:16:18,744 --> 00:16:21,614
I think about it often.

251
00:16:21,614 --> 00:16:23,249
None of this is real.

252
00:16:25,751 --> 00:16:27,854
You're trying to manipulate me.

253
00:16:30,456 --> 00:16:32,291
It will never be real.

254
00:16:35,161 --> 00:16:38,798
But you are thinking about that night.

255
00:16:38,798 --> 00:16:40,933
And that's all I need.

256
00:16:42,201 --> 00:16:44,203
I just want to be connected to you.

257
00:16:44,203 --> 00:16:47,340
I offered for you to be my best friend!

258
00:16:53,546 --> 00:16:58,150
But I've realised
if we can't be friends...

259
00:16:59,619 --> 00:17:02,722
then we can be connected in other ways.

260
00:17:06,158 --> 00:17:07,526
How?

261
00:17:10,029 --> 00:17:11,397
You'll see.

262
00:17:13,332 --> 00:17:14,467
In time.

263
00:17:25,144 --> 00:17:28,080
I'm sorry to cut tonight short.

264
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:30,249
But...

265
00:17:30,249 --> 00:17:32,752
your parents and I
have a very important date...

266
00:17:32,752 --> 00:17:34,487
- Jeremiah.
- with destiny.

267
00:17:34,487 --> 00:17:35,388
Jeremiah!

268
00:17:35,388 --> 00:17:38,357
You might want
to find your faithful butler and leave.

269
00:17:39,859 --> 00:17:40,693
Quickly.

270
00:17:44,530 --> 00:17:45,531
Alfred!

271
00:17:57,076 --> 00:17:59,412
The signs lead this way.

272
00:17:59,412 --> 00:18:00,880
Look at the smoke.

273
00:18:00,880 --> 00:18:02,515
Someone restarted production.

274
00:18:21,767 --> 00:18:22,902
My God, Jim.

275
00:18:24,570 --> 00:18:26,038
Look at all of this.

276
00:18:27,073 --> 00:18:27,907
Come on.

277
00:18:34,046 --> 00:18:36,482
- Who's in charge here?
- Tick tock.

278
00:18:36,482 --> 00:18:39,652
The chemical stock,
shall give our Gotham an aftershock.

279
00:18:39,652 --> 00:18:43,222
Tick tock, the chemical stock,
shall give our Gotham an aftershock.

280
00:18:43,222 --> 00:18:44,557
- Tick tock...
- Tick tock...

281
00:18:44,557 --> 00:18:47,493
the chemical stock,
shall give our Gotham an aftershock.

282
00:18:47,493 --> 00:18:48,995
They've been hypnotised.

283
00:18:48,995 --> 00:18:50,296
Tetch.

284
00:18:50,296 --> 00:18:56,102
Tick tock, the chemical stock,
shall give our Gotham an aftershock.

285
00:18:56,102 --> 00:18:58,738
My, my, what a thrill.

286
00:18:58,738 --> 00:19:01,440
Jim Gordon...

287
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:03,509
and the woman he told me to kill.

288
00:19:03,509 --> 00:19:04,977
Brings back memories.

289
00:19:04,977 --> 00:19:08,514
That tea party, so long ago.

290
00:19:08,514 --> 00:19:11,350
But now to order these men
to attack my foe.

291
00:19:14,286 --> 00:19:16,288
All for one and one for all!

292
00:19:16,288 --> 00:19:18,290
Ain't this a grand old ball!

293
00:19:25,865 --> 00:19:31,670
- Jim!
- Ain't this some game!

294
00:19:35,007 --> 00:19:36,175
Give it to me again?

295
00:19:37,810 --> 00:19:41,380
Penguin has been stealing everything
in the city that's not nailed down.

296
00:19:41,380 --> 00:19:44,050
And now he needs
a way of getting it off the island.

297
00:19:45,551 --> 00:19:46,886
And you're helping him?

298
00:19:46,886 --> 00:19:49,555
Well, that's what he thinks.

299
00:19:49,555 --> 00:19:51,524
Barbara, Tabitha was my friend too.

300
00:19:51,524 --> 00:19:53,492
If anything, I want to gut the twerp...

301
00:19:54,693 --> 00:19:55,661
and take his loot.

302
00:19:55,661 --> 00:19:57,797
Except you don't actually have a way out
of Gotham.

303
00:19:57,797 --> 00:19:59,365
I'll find one tonight.

304
00:19:59,365 --> 00:20:00,966
I'll still need your help
moving the stuff.

305
00:20:00,966 --> 00:20:02,902
We can get out of here together.

306
00:20:05,204 --> 00:20:07,206
Away from Jim Gordon.

307
00:20:07,206 --> 00:20:08,974
Rich as Midas.

308
00:20:08,974 --> 00:20:11,043
Penguin dead in a ditch.

309
00:20:11,577 --> 00:20:14,046
Well, aren't we just two single ladies
and a baby

310
00:20:14,046 --> 00:20:16,215
about to kill our sworn enemy together.

311
00:20:17,716 --> 00:20:19,018
What?

312
00:20:19,018 --> 00:20:20,986
It's just you're pregnant.

313
00:20:20,986 --> 00:20:23,155
Don't even start.

314
00:20:26,225 --> 00:20:27,493
Alfred!

315
00:20:28,928 --> 00:20:30,262
Alfred!

316
00:20:32,264 --> 00:20:33,399
Alfred.

317
00:20:33,399 --> 00:20:35,367
- We need to get out of here.
- Ah, Master Bruce.

318
00:20:35,367 --> 00:20:37,336
I was just taking a quiet moment
to tidy up.

319
00:20:37,336 --> 00:20:39,405
We need to go. The bombs.

320
00:20:39,405 --> 00:20:41,674
- What bombs?
- These bombs.

321
00:20:43,042 --> 00:20:45,010
No need for roughhousing, sir.

322
00:20:47,680 --> 00:20:48,914
There has to be a way.

323
00:20:50,382 --> 00:20:51,951
Alfred,
you'd do anything to protect me, right?

324
00:20:51,951 --> 00:20:53,285
Absolutely, sir.

325
00:20:53,285 --> 00:20:55,054
There's a gas leak. In the kitchen.

326
00:20:55,054 --> 00:20:57,256
It's only a matter of time
before this whole place goes up.

327
00:20:57,256 --> 00:20:58,691
A gas leak?

328
00:20:58,691 --> 00:20:59,925
Where are your parents?
Where's our guest?

329
00:20:59,925 --> 00:21:02,595
I've already warned them.
I know a way out. Come on!

330
00:21:33,058 --> 00:21:34,160
Alfred!

331
00:21:35,661 --> 00:21:36,595
Alfred.

332
00:21:39,899 --> 00:21:42,168
- Oh, bloody hell.
- Don't move.

333
00:21:43,602 --> 00:21:44,637
Do you...

334
00:21:45,838 --> 00:21:47,740
Oh, yeah, I remember everything.

335
00:21:48,741 --> 00:21:50,109
Clear as day.

336
00:21:50,109 --> 00:21:53,245
Let me tell you, if ever I see
that Jervis Tetch character again,

337
00:21:53,245 --> 00:21:55,414
I'll stick that watch so far up his...

338
00:21:56,582 --> 00:21:57,650
his nose.

339
00:21:58,851 --> 00:21:59,919
How about you?

340
00:22:00,953 --> 00:22:02,521
You all right?

341
00:22:02,521 --> 00:22:03,756
Yeah, I'm all right.

342
00:22:05,291 --> 00:22:06,425
The manor...

343
00:22:07,960 --> 00:22:09,528
Don't you worry about that now, son.

344
00:22:10,596 --> 00:22:11,697
Come on. Help me up.

345
00:22:14,867 --> 00:22:15,935
Oh, your leg's hurt.

346
00:22:15,935 --> 00:22:17,937
Yes, but it's not broken.

347
00:22:30,616 --> 00:22:31,884
I thought I lost you.

348
00:22:32,985 --> 00:22:33,852
Me?

349
00:22:35,487 --> 00:22:37,289
Never, Master Bruce.

350
00:22:40,392 --> 00:22:41,227
Go on.

351
00:22:42,728 --> 00:22:44,129
You know where he's gonna be at.

352
00:22:46,398 --> 00:22:47,233
Go.

353
00:22:59,845 --> 00:23:01,547
If you're here,

354
00:23:01,547 --> 00:23:03,882
Jeremiah must still be alive.

355
00:23:05,184 --> 00:23:08,153
And if you're here,
I'm guessing you found our test subjects,

356
00:23:08,153 --> 00:23:10,656
all boiled and bubbled.

357
00:23:11,890 --> 00:23:12,858
What's he planning?

358
00:23:13,859 --> 00:23:16,428
It's a surprise, don't you know?

359
00:23:16,428 --> 00:23:19,231
A real killer.

360
00:23:19,231 --> 00:23:24,236
Shall I hypnotise our friends here
and have them slit each other's necks?

361
00:23:24,236 --> 00:23:25,704
Nix.

362
00:23:25,704 --> 00:23:26,772
Better check with the boss.

363
00:23:27,773 --> 00:23:30,109
He might have other ideas.

364
00:23:34,847 --> 00:23:36,949
I'm sorry I got you involved in this.

365
00:23:36,949 --> 00:23:39,118
Don't be. I knew
what I was getting myself into.

366
00:23:39,118 --> 00:23:42,454
- I know, but, Lee...
- Jim,

367
00:23:42,454 --> 00:23:46,225
whatever you want to tell me,
save it till we're out of here.

368
00:23:46,225 --> 00:23:47,526
Fair enough.

369
00:23:47,526 --> 00:23:49,928
We need to find
out what Valeska's planning.

370
00:23:51,196 --> 00:23:52,298
Hey, Tetch.

371
00:23:53,632 --> 00:23:55,067
You know, it's funny.

372
00:23:55,934 --> 00:23:59,271
I never figured you
for Jeremiah's errand boy.

373
00:23:59,271 --> 00:24:00,639
Oh, Captain.

374
00:24:00,639 --> 00:24:02,408
No errands do I run.

375
00:24:02,408 --> 00:24:04,977
This is simply a way for me
to have some fun.

376
00:24:05,978 --> 00:24:07,146
Tell yourself that.

377
00:24:08,881 --> 00:24:12,985
What are you when you would take away
your games and your rhymes?

378
00:24:12,985 --> 00:24:16,255
Nothing but a second-rater
with a really silly hat.

379
00:24:16,255 --> 00:24:17,389
Shut up.

380
00:24:20,893 --> 00:24:22,561
Beautiful. Beautiful.

381
00:24:24,063 --> 00:24:27,733
Lee Thompkins, you do intrigue me so.

382
00:24:27,733 --> 00:24:30,969
First, you were a doctor,

383
00:24:30,969 --> 00:24:33,238
then the Narrows Queen.

384
00:24:33,238 --> 00:24:35,607
Tell me, please do,

385
00:24:35,607 --> 00:24:40,012
are you running from your past
when you become someone new?

386
00:25:02,701 --> 00:25:04,803
When I found Jeremiah,

387
00:25:04,803 --> 00:25:07,639
he had a bunch of crazies
digging this tunnel for him.

388
00:25:08,040 --> 00:25:11,009
Well, that certainly fills me
with confidence.

389
00:25:12,311 --> 00:25:13,278
You hear that?

390
00:25:21,820 --> 00:25:24,356
- Alfred.
- Selina.

391
00:25:24,356 --> 00:25:25,457
What are you doing here?

392
00:25:26,525 --> 00:25:28,293
And with that?

393
00:25:28,293 --> 00:25:31,630
I should ask you the same thing.
What's down that tunnel?

394
00:25:31,630 --> 00:25:33,799
Well, it was Wayne Manor
till Jeremiah blew it up.

395
00:25:34,867 --> 00:25:37,002
He sealed the only way out of Gotham.

396
00:25:37,002 --> 00:25:41,473
No. Jeremiah is not alive.
I saw him die right here.

397
00:25:41,473 --> 00:25:42,875
Yeah, well, you're wrong.

398
00:25:42,875 --> 00:25:44,810
We all were.

399
00:25:44,810 --> 00:25:47,346
And now, he's embarked
on some madcap scheme

400
00:25:47,346 --> 00:25:49,715
where he's re-enacting the night
Bruce's parents were killed.

401
00:25:49,715 --> 00:25:52,317
- Where's Bruce?
- He's gone after Jeremiah.

402
00:25:53,685 --> 00:25:55,020
He could use your help.

403
00:25:58,090 --> 00:25:59,425
Wait.

404
00:25:59,425 --> 00:26:02,494
You think that because
I did not kill Jeremiah

405
00:26:02,494 --> 00:26:04,863
does not mean that I won't kill you.

406
00:26:04,863 --> 00:26:09,101
- Selina.
- You killed my friend Tabitha.

407
00:26:10,235 --> 00:26:12,604
- You deserve to die.
- Selina.

408
00:26:14,206 --> 00:26:15,574
Just put the knife down.

409
00:26:17,743 --> 00:26:18,911
Bruce needs you.

410
00:26:35,727 --> 00:26:37,963
I suppose I should thank you.

411
00:26:37,963 --> 00:26:41,767
Or you could help me to the Green Zone.

412
00:26:41,767 --> 00:26:44,570
Of course. It's that way.

413
00:27:01,320 --> 00:27:02,788
Jeremiah!

414
00:27:04,256 --> 00:27:05,757
Show yourself!

415
00:27:33,785 --> 00:27:34,653
Ole!

416
00:27:35,687 --> 00:27:37,523
Hola, Bruce.

417
00:27:37,523 --> 00:27:40,158
Well, here we are,

418
00:27:40,158 --> 00:27:46,198
the theatre where your Mummy and Daddy
took you to see The Mark of Zorro.

419
00:27:48,634 --> 00:27:51,370
I had heard you were obsessed
with this man as a child.

420
00:27:51,370 --> 00:27:54,273
I wonder what was
it that intrigued you so?

421
00:27:54,273 --> 00:27:57,709
Was it the fact that he struck fear
into the hearts of his enemy?

422
00:28:02,214 --> 00:28:03,782
En garde!

423
00:28:05,484 --> 00:28:07,185
Take that, you villain.

424
00:28:08,220 --> 00:28:09,621
Vagabond.

425
00:28:11,356 --> 00:28:12,524
Scoundrel.

426
00:28:20,132 --> 00:28:21,466
Warned you.

427
00:28:22,467 --> 00:28:25,504
Perhaps the movie was a bit too effective.

428
00:28:27,339 --> 00:28:30,642
Isn't this the part
where you became frightened?

429
00:28:30,642 --> 00:28:33,145
When you asked your parents to leave?

430
00:28:34,179 --> 00:28:37,182
I wonder what would have happened
if you hadn't done that.

431
00:28:37,182 --> 00:28:40,819
If you had conquered your fear.

432
00:28:40,819 --> 00:28:43,922
Maybe your parents would still be alive.

433
00:28:49,695 --> 00:28:54,933
Well, on to the last and final stop
down memory lane.

434
00:29:01,707 --> 00:29:02,674
Stop!

435
00:29:04,076 --> 00:29:05,243
Stop!

436
00:29:05,243 --> 00:29:09,014
- That's far enough, Bruce.
- Jeremiah.

437
00:29:09,014 --> 00:29:11,617
- You don't have to do this.
- But I...

438
00:29:12,851 --> 00:29:13,785
I do.

439
00:29:15,020 --> 00:29:18,357
You see, I came to this realisation.

440
00:29:19,925 --> 00:29:23,362
I realised that no matter what I did
to bond us,

441
00:29:23,362 --> 00:29:26,365
some random gunman in an alley
would be the man

442
00:29:26,365 --> 00:29:28,300
who you were tied to the most.

443
00:29:29,301 --> 00:29:32,237
The man you saw when you close your eyes.

444
00:29:33,438 --> 00:29:36,308
I want to be the star of the show.

445
00:29:38,377 --> 00:29:41,980
So if I can't have you as a brother
bonded by love...

446
00:29:43,982 --> 00:29:46,918
then we'll just have to be bonded
by hatred.

447
00:29:46,918 --> 00:29:50,589
And you think killing two people
that look like my parents will do that?

448
00:29:51,790 --> 00:29:52,891
It won't.

449
00:29:52,891 --> 00:29:54,960
Well, then it's a good thing
I already put a bullet

450
00:29:54,960 --> 00:29:57,663
in both of their fraudulent skulls.

451
00:29:59,164 --> 00:30:00,832
Oh, you're confused.

452
00:30:00,832 --> 00:30:03,068
You're wondering if I already shot them,

453
00:30:03,068 --> 00:30:06,338
then who's this lovely couple?

454
00:30:07,906 --> 00:30:09,941
Thomas, Martha...

455
00:30:10,942 --> 00:30:12,978
why don't you turn around?

456
00:30:26,525 --> 00:30:27,359
Jim!

457
00:30:28,860 --> 00:30:30,195
I know.

458
00:30:30,195 --> 00:30:33,465
See, over the course
of our little adventure,

459
00:30:33,465 --> 00:30:37,936
fate brought to me James Gordon
and Leslie Thompkins,

460
00:30:37,936 --> 00:30:39,504
and I thought to myself...

461
00:30:41,339 --> 00:30:42,507
why not...

462
00:30:43,875 --> 00:30:48,880
why not kill the man who you think of
as your second father figure?

463
00:30:48,880 --> 00:30:54,853
And your dear, dear,
dear friend Lee Thompkins.

464
00:30:55,854 --> 00:30:57,823
And when I do,

465
00:30:57,823 --> 00:31:00,892
finally, you and I will be bound together.

466
00:31:00,892 --> 00:31:02,027
Because you see...

467
00:31:07,999 --> 00:31:12,204
re-unification with the mainland
hangs on by a thread.

468
00:31:12,204 --> 00:31:13,972
Those fireworks go off

469
00:31:13,972 --> 00:31:16,808
and toxic chemicals rain down
onto the city,

470
00:31:16,808 --> 00:31:18,009
and the government...

471
00:31:19,010 --> 00:31:20,512
cuts us adrift for good.

472
00:31:27,319 --> 00:31:28,153
Jeremiah.

473
00:31:29,821 --> 00:31:30,655
Don't.

474
00:31:32,524 --> 00:31:34,526
The piece de resistance.

475
00:31:35,560 --> 00:31:37,162
One last thing.

476
00:31:37,162 --> 00:31:39,831
I had Jervis Tetch hypnotise them,

477
00:31:39,831 --> 00:31:44,736
so that they'll wake up the moment
these beautiful pearls hit the ground.

478
00:31:46,104 --> 00:31:48,874
I want you to see them realise
what I've done to them

479
00:31:48,874 --> 00:31:51,610
as the life drains from their bodies.

480
00:31:53,111 --> 00:31:57,682
Never forget, this is all for you, Bruce.

481
00:31:57,682 --> 00:31:58,917
No!

482
00:32:06,424 --> 00:32:07,726
Selina, the pearls!

483
00:32:19,871 --> 00:32:21,306
Ecco!

484
00:32:21,306 --> 00:32:22,440
Now!

485
00:32:30,415 --> 00:32:31,950
We need to stop the fireworks.
They're gonna...

486
00:32:31,950 --> 00:32:35,220
I know. You go after Jeremiah and Ecco.
I'll take the truck.

487
00:32:39,758 --> 00:32:41,660
There's no way to stop them all.

488
00:32:41,660 --> 00:32:43,795
Get to Harvey.

489
00:32:44,229 --> 00:32:47,065
Warn the people in the Green Zone
to get to cover.

490
00:32:47,065 --> 00:32:49,000
What are you...

491
00:32:49,000 --> 00:32:50,769
Jim!

492
00:32:58,643 --> 00:33:00,779
Jeremiah!

493
00:33:00,779 --> 00:33:02,747
Face me!

494
00:33:02,747 --> 00:33:03,982
Here, Bruce.

495
00:33:45,523 --> 00:33:46,658
Jeremiah!

496
00:33:48,526 --> 00:33:50,395
This ends.

497
00:33:50,395 --> 00:33:51,529
Tonight.

498
00:33:52,664 --> 00:33:53,899
No.

499
00:33:53,899 --> 00:33:56,902
No, Bruce. Now it begins.

500
00:34:13,752 --> 00:34:19,891
Yes. You feel it.
The connection between us.

501
00:34:19,891 --> 00:34:21,226
You do.

502
00:34:21,226 --> 00:34:24,596
Don't you? Bruce, you feel it.

503
00:34:24,596 --> 00:34:26,031
Tell me you feel it.

504
00:34:29,534 --> 00:34:31,569
You mean nothing to me.

505
00:34:36,408 --> 00:34:39,177
Why don't you understand?

506
00:34:41,446 --> 00:34:43,949
You need me.

507
00:34:43,949 --> 00:34:47,385
I'm the answer to your life's question.

508
00:34:47,385 --> 00:34:49,754
Without me, you're just a joke...

509
00:34:52,390 --> 00:34:54,960
without a punch line.

510
00:35:54,853 --> 00:36:00,759
After all this time,
you've come to me for help.

511
00:36:00,759 --> 00:36:04,362
After allowing Strange to put a chip
into my brain.

512
00:36:04,362 --> 00:36:06,464
Attempting to sell me out to Gordon.

513
00:36:06,464 --> 00:36:07,999
And after naming...

514
00:36:09,834 --> 00:36:12,203
a dog after me.

515
00:36:12,203 --> 00:36:16,941
First of all, I am very fond of that dog.

516
00:36:16,941 --> 00:36:21,980
Secondly, I had Hugo Strange
save your life.

517
00:36:21,980 --> 00:36:26,785
Thirdly, do you really think
I didn't have plans to save you

518
00:36:26,785 --> 00:36:29,054
from Jim Gordon?

519
00:36:31,689 --> 00:36:34,959
You always have an answer for everything,
don't you, Oswald?

520
00:36:34,959 --> 00:36:38,563
We have been through all of this before.

521
00:36:38,563 --> 00:36:43,134
I've tried to kill you.
You've tried to kill me.

522
00:36:43,134 --> 00:36:47,372
But here we are in this room. Together.

523
00:36:49,841 --> 00:36:52,243
It means fate has different plans for us.

524
00:36:57,482 --> 00:36:59,384
What are these plans?

525
00:36:59,584 --> 00:37:02,420
Haven't you realised what Gotham is yet?

526
00:37:02,720 --> 00:37:05,490
It is no longer a city.

527
00:37:05,490 --> 00:37:06,758
It is a prison.

528
00:37:08,893 --> 00:37:10,562
And I think it's time we escaped.

529
00:37:26,077 --> 00:37:27,579
You heard the news?

530
00:37:27,579 --> 00:37:30,014
Everybody's talking about it.

531
00:37:30,014 --> 00:37:31,749
Reunification isn't happening.

532
00:37:31,749 --> 00:37:34,052
Word of the chemical spill
reached the mainland.

533
00:37:34,052 --> 00:37:38,256
No action until the government
can determine if Gotham is safe.

534
00:37:38,256 --> 00:37:40,058
I figure at least a couple of months.

535
00:37:41,593 --> 00:37:43,428
You don't sound surprised.

536
00:37:43,795 --> 00:37:44,796
Guess, I'm not.

537
00:37:46,931 --> 00:37:48,633
Could've been much worse.

538
00:37:48,633 --> 00:37:49,868
You stopped that.

539
00:37:51,202 --> 00:37:53,771
Every time I think
we're turning things around, I look up,

540
00:37:53,771 --> 00:37:55,106
right back where we started.

541
00:38:06,818 --> 00:38:10,421
What were you about to say to me
when Tetch had us?

542
00:38:16,427 --> 00:38:17,328
I don't know.

543
00:38:18,630 --> 00:38:20,498
I guess I...

544
00:38:20,498 --> 00:38:21,633
would have said...

545
00:38:23,168 --> 00:38:24,936
what I said the last time
we saw each other.

546
00:38:29,407 --> 00:38:30,742
I wish I could go back.

547
00:38:33,111 --> 00:38:34,245
Do things differently.

548
00:38:35,346 --> 00:38:36,314
Better.

549
00:38:40,685 --> 00:38:42,687
It feels like a long time ago.

550
00:38:42,687 --> 00:38:43,821
Nothing's changed.

551
00:38:44,856 --> 00:38:46,191
But it has, Jim.

552
00:38:48,793 --> 00:38:51,262
- That was a mistake.
- A mistake?

553
00:38:51,262 --> 00:38:53,531
Put yourself in my shoes.

554
00:38:53,531 --> 00:38:55,800
After everything you said,
suddenly you're having a baby

555
00:38:55,800 --> 00:38:57,669
with Barbara, of all people.

556
00:39:01,940 --> 00:39:03,107
But it's not just that.

557
00:39:04,509 --> 00:39:07,345
You talk about doing things differently
and I keep thinking...

558
00:39:09,314 --> 00:39:10,882
what if we hadn't lost ours?

559
00:39:19,290 --> 00:39:20,525
What are you doing here, Lee?

560
00:39:24,128 --> 00:39:25,230
I don't know.

561
00:39:26,831 --> 00:39:29,200
I know you've taken on so much, and...

562
00:39:30,835 --> 00:39:33,171
and I want to be understanding, but...

563
00:39:34,639 --> 00:39:36,140
you let me down, Jim.

564
00:39:40,044 --> 00:39:41,145
I'm sorry.

565
00:39:46,017 --> 00:39:47,652
What does that mean?

566
00:39:48,553 --> 00:39:50,154
For us?

567
00:39:50,154 --> 00:39:51,589
I don't know.

568
00:39:53,524 --> 00:39:57,328
Can't change the past,
so I guess we just have to live with it.

569
00:40:00,765 --> 00:40:02,333
No, Lee...

570
00:40:24,355 --> 00:40:27,625
I can't believe he's still alive.

571
00:40:28,893 --> 00:40:31,562
They've been doing scans,
and he has no brain activity.

572
00:40:33,097 --> 00:40:34,432
He's no longer a threat.

573
00:40:37,402 --> 00:40:38,403
To either of us.

574
00:40:46,110 --> 00:40:47,645
Thank you for coming to help me.

575
00:40:51,916 --> 00:40:54,652
That night your parents were killed,
I should have done something.

576
00:40:57,221 --> 00:40:58,723
Selina, you've done enough.

577
00:41:10,668 --> 00:41:12,603
It's not much, but it's home.

578
00:41:12,603 --> 00:41:15,006
I've been looking
through your treasure trove.

579
00:41:15,006 --> 00:41:17,075
You've been a very naughty boy.

580
00:41:17,075 --> 00:41:18,409
Barbara?

581
00:41:18,409 --> 00:41:19,477
How did you...

582
00:41:21,245 --> 00:41:22,280
Selina?

583
00:41:24,148 --> 00:41:28,252
She and I were gonna go murder-halfsies
to get you back for Tabitha,

584
00:41:28,252 --> 00:41:32,657
but it seems I will have to do the dirty
work myself, as usual.

585
00:41:32,657 --> 00:41:33,691
Oh, my God.

586
00:41:35,660 --> 00:41:36,861
You're pregnant.

587
00:41:39,597 --> 00:41:41,165
How could you possibly know that?

588
00:41:41,165 --> 00:41:42,667
Look at you.

589
00:41:42,667 --> 00:41:44,302
She's glowing.

590
00:41:44,302 --> 00:41:46,104
You're glowing.

591
00:41:46,104 --> 00:41:47,772
How very observant of you.

592
00:41:47,772 --> 00:41:49,273
Adieu, Oswald.

593
00:41:49,273 --> 00:41:50,808
Wait.

594
00:41:50,808 --> 00:41:53,344
Come with us.

595
00:41:53,344 --> 00:41:56,180
- What?
- Yes.

596
00:41:56,180 --> 00:41:58,816
I killed Tabitha.

597
00:41:58,816 --> 00:42:00,284
You're angry.

598
00:42:00,284 --> 00:42:01,853
You want revenge.

599
00:42:01,853 --> 00:42:07,358
But do you really want to raise your child
in a toxic waste war zone?

600
00:42:08,626 --> 00:42:10,061
Come with us.

601
00:42:11,829 --> 00:42:14,699
Are you telling me you found a way out
of Gotham?

602
00:42:14,699 --> 00:42:15,900
Ed did.

603
00:42:18,836 --> 00:42:21,406
- It's a submarine.
- A submarine?

604
00:42:21,406 --> 00:42:24,242
It can track mines
in the river using sonar.

605
00:42:27,345 --> 00:42:28,846
So where's this submarine?

606
00:42:34,385 --> 00:42:35,753
We have to build it.

607
00:42:35,753 --> 00:42:37,054
Yeah, I'm gonna shoot you.

608
00:42:39,991 --> 00:42:40,925
God.

609
00:42:42,260 --> 00:42:44,228
What is happening to me?

610
00:42:44,228 --> 00:42:45,863
- Perhaps...
- Shut up!

611
00:42:45,863 --> 00:42:47,498
That was a rhetorical question.

612
00:42:52,203 --> 00:42:53,905
Fine.

613
00:42:53,905 --> 00:42:57,241
I won't shoot you
for the sake of my child.

614
00:42:57,775 --> 00:42:59,777
But I will never forgive you.

615
00:42:59,777 --> 00:43:01,846
Of course.

616
00:43:01,846 --> 00:43:03,347
I understand.

617
00:43:08,352 --> 00:43:09,620
Call me when it's done.

618
00:43:09,620 --> 00:43:12,023
- So who's the lucky father?
- Shut up!
